	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "ESP32-C3-WROOM-02, derived for Aethelgard (AET-WO-4411 D4) from KiCad 10.0.7 RF_Module:ESP32-C3-WROOM-02 (kicad-footprints tag 10.0.7, sha256 2eb3ceb2324d141108b2f5a46480e74117f3f2181b36f0a5dd9791efb847816b), CC-BY-SA-4.0 with KiCad's design exception. Changes, each with its reason: (1) the keepout zone: KiCad's one zone on all 32 copper layers, 5 mm around the antenna, is replaced by one zone per copper layer (F.Cu and B.Cu here; the emitter adds one per inner layer), each the antenna area only, 18 x 6 mm (datasheet v1.7 p. 37, Fig. 11-1): the gate refuses a zone naming a layer the board lacks, and the 15 mm clearance beyond the antenna (Hardware Design Guidelines Fig. 21) is judged by the gate from the part row, never from a zone; (2) the ground pad's 12 vias at 0.2 mm drill are replaced by 4 at the engine's 0.6 mm pad and 0.3 mm drill, at the crossings of the 3 x 3 land pattern's gaps (p. 37, Fig. 11-1, 1.1 mm pitch): 12 at 0.3 mm on the 0.55 mm pitch would leave 0.25 mm between holes; (3) the courtyard: KiCad's outline around its 5 mm zone becomes the rectangle around the module's body, pads and antenna area, so the keepout lies inside it; (4) the silkscreen beside and above the antenna area, and the pin 1 triangle crossing it, are removed: the antenna area overhangs the board edge (D2), where silkscreen meets the edge; (5) KiCad's keep-out dimension drawings and texts on Cmts.User are removed with its zone.")
	(tags "ESP32-C3 WROOM-02 espressif")
